    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for the Zurich Zebras prioritizes volume and high-leverage spots despite a daunting slate of opposing arms. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.33) is our strongest play today, capitalizing on his leadoff role and a favorable matchup against Abbott; while his platoon splits are usually a concern, the volume of high-percentage scoring opportunities from the #1 hole outweighs the park and skill factors. **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) also offers significant value, as his dynamic platoon advantage against Lorenzen boosts his ceiling well above his base projection, making him a critical piece of our offensive engine. **Kazuma Okamoto** (60.22) rounds out our top-tier targets, benefiting from a soft matchup against M\u00e1rquez, whose 5.58 xERA is the most exploitable figure on the board today.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision was navigating the bench, specifically regarding **Carson Benge** (43.14). While he narrowly missed the cut, he remained outside the starting rotation because the matchup against Tolle presented too significant a platoon hurdle, suppressing his efficiency score below our threshold for starting production. We also remain cautious regarding the heavy concentration of elite pitching across the board\u2014facing Skubal twice with **Trea Turner** (56.81) and **Kyle Schwarber** (55.06), as well as Skenes against **Christian Yelich** (54.28)\u2014which introduces notable variance. Keep a close eye on the confirmed lineups for **Yordan Alvarez** and **Casey Schmitt**; should those projected spots shift, we will need to re-evaluate our exposure to these high-strikeout starters to ensure we aren't chasing empty efficiency in a category as volatile as AVG.",
